u}$ channel. Employing recent experimental data from LHCb regarding $B^+ \to K^+ \tau \bar{
u}$, $B^0 \to \pi^0 \tau \bar{
u}$, $B^0 \to \pi^0 \tau \bar{
u}$, and the charge asymmetry in $B^0 \to \pi^0 \tau \bar{
u}$, we determine that any such NP couplings must be approximately an order of magnitude weaker than those in the SM. Consequently, these potential effects in $B^0 \to \pi^0 \tau \bar{
u}$ are suppressed to a level where their ability to significantly alter the WL dark matter relic density is negligible.

